msgstr ""
"Delta multiplicado por um float. O resultado é arredondado para o múltiplo "
"mais próximo de timedelta.resolution usando round-half-to-even."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:367
msgid "``f = t2 / t3``"
msgstr "``f = t2 / t3``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:367
msgid ""
"Division (3) of overall duration ``t2`` by interval unit ``t3``. Returns a :"
"class:`float` object."
msgstr ""
"Divisão (3) da duração total ``t2`` pela unidade de intervalo ``t3``. "
"Devolve um objeto :class:`float`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:371
msgid "``t1 = t2 / f or t1 = t2 / i``"
msgstr "``t1 = t2 / f or t1 = t2 / i``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:371
msgid ""
"Delta divided by a float or an int. The result is rounded to the nearest "
"multiple of timedelta.resolution using round-half-to-even."
msgstr ""
"Delta dividido por um float ou um inteiro. O resultado é arredondado para o "
"múltiplo mais próximo de timedelta.resolution usando round-half-to-even."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:375
msgid "``t1 = t2 // i`` or ``t1 = t2 // t3``"
msgstr "``t1 = t2 // i`` ou ``t1 = t2 // t3``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:375
msgid ""
"The floor is computed and the remainder (if any) is thrown away. In the "
"second case, an integer is returned. (3)"
msgstr ""
"O piso é calculado e o resto (se existir) é descartado. No segundo caso, é "
"devolvido um inteiro. (3)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:379
msgid "``t1 = t2 % t3``"
msgstr "``t1 = t2 % t3``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:379
msgid "The remainder is computed as a :class:`timedelta` object. (3)"
msgstr "O resto é calculado como um objeto :class:`timedelta`. (3)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:382
msgid "``q, r = divmod(t1, t2)``"
msgstr "``q, r = divmod(t1, t2)``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:382
msgid ""
"Computes the quotient and the remainder: ``q = t1 // t2`` (3) and ``r = t1 % "
"t2``. ``q`` is an integer and ``r`` is a :class:`timedelta` object."
msgstr ""
"Calcula o quociente e o resto: ``q = t1 // t2`` (3) e ``r = t1 % t2``. ``q`` "
"é um inteiro e ``r`` é um objeto :class:`timedelta`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:387
msgid "``+t1``"
msgstr "``+t1``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:387
msgid "Returns a :class:`timedelta` object with the same value. (2)"
msgstr "Devolve um objeto :class:`timedelta` com o mesmo valor. (2)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:390
msgid "``-t1``"
msgstr "``-t1``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:390
msgid ""
"Equivalent to ``timedelta(-t1.days, -t1.seconds, -t1.microseconds)``, and to "
"``t1 * -1``. (1)(4)"
msgstr ""
"Equivalente a ``timedelta(-t1.days, -t1.seconds, -t1.microseconds)``, e a "
"``t1 * -1``. (1)(4)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:394
msgid "``abs(t)``"
msgstr "``abs(t)``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:394
msgid ""
"Equivalent to ``+t`` when ``t.days >= 0``, and to ``-t`` when ``t.days < "
"0``. (2)"
msgstr ""
"Equivalente a ``+t`` quando ``t.days >= 0``, e a ``-t`` quando ``t.days < "
"0``. (2)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:397
msgid "``str(t)``"
msgstr "``str(t)``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:397
msgid ""
"Returns a string in the form ``[D day[s], ][H]H:MM:SS[.UUUUUU]``, where D is "
"negative for negative ``t``. (5)"
msgstr ""
"Devolve uma string no formato ``[D day[s], ][H]H:MM:SS[.UUUUUU]``, onde D é "
"negativo para ``t`` negativo. (5)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:401
msgid "``repr(t)``"
msgstr "``repr(t)``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:401
msgid ""
"Returns a string representation of the :class:`timedelta` object as a "
"constructor call with canonical attribute values."
msgstr ""
"Devolve uma representação em string do objeto :class:`timedelta` como uma "
"chamada de construtor com valores de atributos canónicos."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:406 ../../library/datetime.rst:685
#: ../../library/datetime.rst:2796
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr "Notas:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:409
msgid "This is exact but may overflow."
msgstr "Isto é exato, mas pode causar overflow."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:412
msgid "This is exact and cannot overflow."
msgstr "Isto é exato e não pode causar overflow."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:415
msgid "Division by zero raises :exc:`ZeroDivisionError`."
msgstr "Divisão por zero gera um :exc:`ZeroDivisionError`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:418
msgid "``-timedelta.max`` is not representable as a :class:`timedelta` object."
msgstr ""
"``-timedelta.max`` não é representável como um objeto :class:`timedelta`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:421
msgid ""
"String representations of :class:`timedelta` objects are normalized "
"similarly to their internal representation. This leads to somewhat unusual "
"results for negative timedeltas. For example::"
msgstr ""
"As representações em string de objetos :class:`timedelta` são normalizadas "
"de forma semelhante à sua representação interna. Isto leva a resultados algo "
"invulgares para timedeltas negativos. Por exemplo:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:425
msgid ""
">>> timedelta(hours=-5)\n"
"datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=68400)\n"
">>> print(_)\n"
"-1 day, 19:00:00"
msgstr ""
">>> timedelta(hours=-5)\n"
"datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=68400)\n"
">>> print(_)\n"
"-1 day, 19:00:00"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:431
msgid ""
"The expression ``t2 - t3`` will always be equal to the expression ``t2 + (-"
"t3)`` except when t3 is equal to ``timedelta.max``; in that case the former "
"will produce a result while the latter will overflow."
msgstr ""
"A expressão ``t2 - t3`` será sempre igual à expressão ``t2 + (-t3)`` exceto "
"quando t3 for igual a ``timedelta.max``; nesse caso, a primeira produzirá um "
"resultado enquanto a segunda causará overflow."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:435
msgid ""
"In addition to the operations listed above, :class:`timedelta` objects "
"support certain additions and subtractions with :class:`date` and :class:`."
"datetime` objects (see below)."
msgstr ""
"Além das operações listadas acima, os objetos :class:`timedelta` suportam "
"certas adições e subtrações com objetos :class:`date` e :class:`.datetime` "
"(ver abaixo)."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:439
msgid ""
"Floor division and true division of a :class:`timedelta` object by another :"
"class:`!timedelta` object are now supported, as are remainder operations and "
"the :func:`divmod` function. True division and multiplication of a :class:`!"
"timedelta` object by a :class:`float` object are now supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:445
msgid ":class:`timedelta` objects support equality and order comparisons."
msgstr ""
"Os objetos :class:`timedelta` suportam comparações de igualdade e ordem."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:447
msgid ""
"In Boolean contexts, a :class:`timedelta` object is considered to be true if "
"and only if it isn't equal to ``timedelta(0)``."
msgstr ""
"Em contextos booleanos, um objeto :class:`timedelta` é considerado "
"verdadeiro se e somente se não for igual a ``timedelta(0)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:450 ../../library/datetime.rst:727
#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1366 ../../library/datetime.rst:1995
msgid "Instance methods:"
msgstr "Métodos de instância:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:454
msgid ""
"Return the total number of seconds contained in the duration. Equivalent to "
"``td / timedelta(seconds=1)``. For interval units other than seconds, use "
"the division form directly (for example, ``td / timedelta(microseconds=1)``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:458
msgid ""
"Note that for very large time intervals (greater than 270 years on most "
"platforms) this method will lose microsecond accuracy."
msgstr ""
"Note que para intervalos de tempo muito grandes (maiores que 270 anos na "
"maioria das plataformas) este método perderá precisão de microsegundos."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:465
msgid "Examples of usage: :class:`!timedelta`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:467
msgid "An additional example of normalization::"
msgstr "Um exemplo adicional de normalização:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:469
msgid ""
">>> # Components of another_year add up to exactly 365 days\n"
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> year = dt.timedelta(days=365)\n"
">>> another_year = dt.timedelta(weeks=40, days=84, hours=23,\n"
"...                             minutes=50, seconds=600)\n"
">>> year == another_year\n"
"True\n"
">>> year.total_seconds()\n"
"31536000.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:479
msgid "Examples of :class:`timedelta` arithmetic::"
msgstr "Exemplos de aritmética :class:`timedelta`:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:481
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> year = dt.timedelta(days=365)\n"
">>> ten_years = 10 * year\n"
">>> ten_years\n"
"datetime.timedelta(days=3650)\n"
">>> ten_years.days // 365\n"
"10\n"
">>> nine_years = ten_years - year\n"
">>> nine_years\n"
"datetime.timedelta(days=3285)\n"
">>> three_years = nine_years // 3\n"
">>> three_years, three_years.days // 365\n"
"(datetime.timedelta(days=1095), 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:499
msgid ":class:`!date` objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:501
msgid ""
"A :class:`date` object represents a date (year, month and day) in an "
"idealized calendar, the current Gregorian calendar indefinitely extended in "
"both directions."
msgstr ""
"Um objeto :class:`date` representa uma data (ano, mês e dia) num calendário "
"idealizado, o atual calendário gregoriano estendido indefinidamente em ambas "
"as direções."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:505
msgid ""
"January 1 of year 1 is called day number 1, January 2 of year 1 is called "
"day number 2, and so on. [#]_"
msgstr ""
"O dia 1 de janeiro do ano 1 é chamado dia número 1, o dia 2 de janeiro do "
"ano 1 é chamado dia número 2, e assim sucessivamente. [#]_"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:510
msgid ""
"All arguments are required. Arguments must be integers, in the following "
"ranges:"
msgstr ""
"Todos os argumentos são obrigatórios. Os argumentos devem ser inteiros, nos "
"seguintes intervalos:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:513
msgid "``MINYEAR <= year <= MAXYEAR``"
msgstr "``MINYEAR <= year <= MAXYEAR``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:514
msgid "``1 <= month <= 12``"
msgstr "``1 <= month <= 12``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:515
msgid "``1 <= day <= number of days in the given month and year``"
msgstr "``1 <= day <= number of days in the given month and year``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:517 ../../library/datetime.rst:948
msgid ""
"If an argument outside those ranges is given, :exc:`ValueError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Se for fornecido um argumento fora desses intervalos, é gerado um :exc:"
"`ValueError`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:520 ../../library/datetime.rst:954
msgid "Other constructors, all class methods:"
msgstr "Outros construtores, todos métodos de classe:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:524
msgid "Return the current local date."
msgstr "Devolve a data local atual."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:526
msgid "This is equivalent to ``date.fromtimestamp(time.time())``."
msgstr "Isto é equivalente a ``date.fromtimestamp(time.time())``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:531
msgid ""
"Return the local date corresponding to the POSIX *timestamp*, such as is "
"returned by :func:`time.time`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:534
msgid ""
"This may raise :exc:`OverflowError`, if the timestamp is out of the range of "
"values supported by the platform C :c:func:`localtime` function, and :exc:"
"`OSError` on :c:func:`localtime` failure. It's common for this to be "
"restricted to years from 1970 through 2038. Note that on non-POSIX systems "
"that include leap seconds in their notion of a timestamp, leap seconds are "
"ignored by :meth:`fromtimestamp`."
msgstr ""
"Isto pode gerar um :exc:`OverflowError` se o timestamp estiver fora do "
"intervalo de valores suportados pela função C :c:func:`localtime` da "
"plataforma, e um :exc:`OSError` em caso de falha da :c:func:`localtime`. É "
"comum que isto esteja restrito aos anos entre 1970 e 2038. Note que em "
"sistemas não-POSIX que incluem segundos bissextos na sua noção de timestamp, "
"os segundos bissextos são ignorados por :meth:`fromtimestamp`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:541
msgid ""
"Raise :exc:`OverflowError` instead of :exc:`ValueError` if the timestamp is "
"out of the range of values supported by the platform C :c:func:`localtime` "
"function. Raise :exc:`OSError` instead of :exc:`ValueError` on :c:func:"
"`localtime` failure."
msgstr ""
"Gera um :exc:`OverflowError` em vez de um :exc:`ValueError` se o timestamp "
"estiver fora do intervalo de valores suportados pela função C :c:func:"
"`localtime` da plataforma. Gera um :exc:`OSError` em vez de um :exc:"
"`ValueError` em caso de falha da :c:func:`localtime`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:547 ../../library/datetime.rst:1042
#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1082
msgid "Accepts any real number as *timestamp*, not only integer or float."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:553
msgid ""
"Return the date corresponding to the proleptic Gregorian *ordinal*, where "
"January 1 of year 1 has ordinal 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:556
msgid ""
":exc:`ValueError` is raised unless ``1 <= ordinal <= date.max.toordinal()``. "
"For any date ``d``, ``date.fromordinal(d.toordinal()) == d``."
msgstr ""
":exc:`ValueError` é gerado a menos que ``1 <= ordinal <= date.max."
"toordinal()``. Para qualquer data ``d``, ``date.fromordinal(d.toordinal()) "
"== d``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:563
msgid ""
"Return a :class:`date` corresponding to a *date_string* given in any valid "
"ISO 8601 format, with the following exceptions:"
msgstr ""
"Devolve um :class:`date` correspondente a uma *date_string* fornecida em "
"qualquer formato ISO 8601 válido, com as seguintes exceções:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:566 ../../library/datetime.rst:1123
msgid ""
"Reduced precision dates are not currently supported (``YYYY-MM``, ``YYYY``)."
msgstr ""
"Datas com precisão reduzida não são atualmente suportadas (``YYYY-MM``, "
"``YYYY``)."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:568 ../../library/datetime.rst:1125
msgid ""
"Extended date representations are not currently supported (``±YYYYYY-MM-"
"DD``)."
msgstr ""
"Representações de datas estendidas não são atualmente suportadas (``±YYYYYY-"
"MM-DD``)."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:570 ../../library/datetime.rst:1127
msgid "Ordinal dates are not currently supported (``YYYY-OOO``)."
msgstr "Datas ordinais não são atualmente suportadas (``YYYY-OOO``)."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:572 ../../library/datetime.rst:1129
#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1604
msgid "Examples::"
msgstr "Exemplos:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:574
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> dt.date.fromisoformat('2019-12-04')\n"
"datetime.date(2019, 12, 4)\n"
">>> dt.date.fromisoformat('20191204')\n"
"datetime.date(2019, 12, 4)\n"
">>> dt.date.fromisoformat('2021-W01-1')\n"
"datetime.date(2021, 1, 4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:583
msgid "Previously, this method only supported the format ``YYYY-MM-DD``."
msgstr "Anteriormente, este método suportava apenas o formato ``YYYY-MM-DD``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:589
msgid ""
"Return a :class:`date` corresponding to the ISO calendar date specified by "
"*year*, *week* and *day*. This is the inverse of the function :meth:`date."
"isocalendar`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:597
msgid ""
"Return a :class:`.date` corresponding to *date_string*, parsed according to "
"*format*. This is equivalent to::"
msgstr ""
"Devolve um :class:`.date` correspondente a *date_string*, analisado de "
"acordo com *format*. Isto é equivalente a:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:600
msgid "date(*(time.strptime(date_string, format)[0:3]))"
msgstr "date(*(time.strptime(date_string, format)[0:3]))"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:602
msgid ""
":exc:`ValueError` is raised if the date_string and format can't be parsed "
"by :func:`time.strptime` or if it returns a value which isn't a time tuple.  "
"See also :ref:`strftime-strptime-behavior` and :meth:`date.fromisoformat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:609 ../../library/datetime.rst:1184
msgid ""
"If *format* specifies a day of month (``%d``) without a year, :exc:"
"`ValueError` is raised.  This is to avoid a quadrennial leap year bug in "
"code seeking to parse only a month and day as the default year used in "
"absence of one in the format is not a leap year. The workaround is to always "
"include a year in your *format*.  If parsing *date_string* values that do "
"not have a year, explicitly add a year that is a leap year before parsing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:617
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> date_string = \"02/29\"\n"
">>> when = dt.date.strptime(f\"{date_string};1984\", \"%m/%d;%Y\")  # Avoids "
"leap year bug.\n"
">>> when.strftime(\"%B %d\")\n"
"'February 29'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:632
msgid "The earliest representable date, ``date(MINYEAR, 1, 1)``."
msgstr "A data representável mais antiga, ``date(MINYEAR, 1, 1)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:637
msgid "The latest representable date, ``date(MAXYEAR, 12, 31)``."
msgstr "A data representável mais recente, ``date(MAXYEAR, 12, 31)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:642
msgid ""
"The smallest possible difference between non-equal date objects, "
"``timedelta(days=1)``."
msgstr ""
"A menor diferença possível entre objetos de data não iguais, "
"``timedelta(days=1)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:650 ../../library/datetime.rst:1225
msgid "Between :const:`MINYEAR` and :const:`MAXYEAR` inclusive."
msgstr "Entre :const:`MINYEAR` e :const:`MAXYEAR`, inclusive."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:655 ../../library/datetime.rst:1230
msgid "Between 1 and 12 inclusive."
msgstr "Entre 1 e 12, inclusive."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:660 ../../library/datetime.rst:1235
msgid "Between 1 and the number of days in the given month of the given year."
msgstr "Entre 1 e o número de dias no mês e ano dados."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:668
msgid "``date2 = date1 + timedelta``"
msgstr "``date2 = date1 + timedelta``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:668
msgid "``date2`` will be ``timedelta.days`` days after ``date1``. (1)"
msgstr "``date2`` será ``timedelta.days`` dias após ``date1``. (1)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:671
msgid "``date2 = date1 - timedelta``"
msgstr "``date2 = date1 - timedelta``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:671
msgid "Computes ``date2`` such that ``date2 + timedelta == date1``. (2)"
msgstr "Calcula ``date2`` de forma que ``date2 + timedelta == date1``. (2)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:674
msgid "``timedelta = date1 - date2``"
msgstr "``timedelta = date1 - date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:674 ../../library/datetime.rst:1284
msgid "\\(3)"
msgstr "(3)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 == date2``"
msgstr "``date1 == date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 != date2``"
msgstr "``date1 != date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:676 ../../library/datetime.rst:1286
msgid "Equality comparison. (4)"
msgstr "Comparação de igualdade. (4)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 < date2``"
msgstr "``date1 < date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 > date2``"
msgstr "``date1 > date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 <= date2``"
msgstr "``date1 <= date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:0
msgid "``date1 >= date2``"
msgstr "``date1 >= date2``"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:679 ../../library/datetime.rst:1289
msgid "Order comparison. (5)"
msgstr "Comparação de ordem. (5)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:688
msgid ""
"*date2* is moved forward in time if ``timedelta.days > 0``, or backward if "
"``timedelta.days < 0``. Afterward ``date2 - date1 == timedelta.days``. "
"``timedelta.seconds`` and ``timedelta.microseconds`` are ignored. :exc:"
"`OverflowError` is raised if ``date2.year`` would be smaller than :const:"
"`MINYEAR` or larger than :const:`MAXYEAR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:695
msgid "``timedelta.seconds`` and ``timedelta.microseconds`` are ignored."
msgstr "``timedelta.seconds`` e ``timedelta.microseconds`` são ignorados."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:698
msgid ""
"This is exact, and cannot overflow. ``timedelta.seconds`` and ``timedelta."
"microseconds`` are 0, and ``date2 + timedelta == date1`` after."
msgstr ""
"Isto é exato e não pode causar overflow. ``timedelta.seconds`` e ``timedelta."
"microseconds`` são 0, e ``date2 + timedelta == date1`` posteriormente."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:702
msgid ":class:`date` objects are equal if they represent the same date."
msgstr "Os objetos :class:`date` são iguais se representarem a mesma data."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:704
msgid ""
":class:`!date` objects that are not also :class:`.datetime` instances are "
"never equal to :class:`!datetime` objects, even if they represent the same "
"date."
msgstr ""
"Os objetos :class:`!date` que não são também instâncias de :class:`."
"datetime` nunca são iguais a objetos :class:`!datetime`, mesmo que "
"representem a mesma data."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:709
msgid ""
"*date1* is considered less than *date2* when *date1* precedes *date2* in "
"time. In other words, ``date1 < date2`` if and only if ``date1.toordinal() < "
"date2.toordinal()``."
msgstr ""
"*data1* é considerada anterior a *data2* quando *data1* precede *data2* no "
"tempo. Em outras palavras, ``date1 < date2`` se e somente se ``date1."
"toordinal() < date2.toordinal()``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:713
msgid ""
"Order comparison between a :class:`date` object that is not also a :class:`."
"datetime` instance and a :class:`!datetime` object raises :exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:717 ../../library/datetime.rst:1357
msgid ""
"Comparison between :class:`.datetime` object and an instance of the :class:"
"`date` subclass that is not a :class:`!datetime` subclass no longer converts "
"the latter to :class:`!date`, ignoring the time part and the time zone. The "
"default behavior can be changed by overriding the special comparison methods "
"in subclasses."
msgstr ""
"A comparação entre um objeto :class:`.datetime` e uma instância de uma "
"subclasse de :class:`date` que não é uma subclasse de :class:`!datetime` já "
"não converte esta última para :class:`!date`, ignorando a parte da hora e o "
"fuso horário. O comportamento predefinido pode ser alterado substituindo os "
"métodos de comparação especiais nas subclasses."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:725
msgid ""
"In Boolean contexts, all :class:`date` objects are considered to be true."
msgstr ""
"Em contextos booleanos, todos os objetos :class:`date` são considerados "
"verdadeiros."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:731
msgid ""
"Return a new :class:`date` object with the same values, but with specified "
"parameters updated."
msgstr ""
"Devolve um novo objeto :class:`date` com os mesmos valores, mas com os "
"parâmetros especificados atualizados."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:734 ../../library/datetime.rst:2041
msgid "Example::"
msgstr "Exemplo::"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:736
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> d = dt.date(2002, 12, 31)\n"
">>> d.replace(day=26)\n"
"datetime.date(2002, 12, 26)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:741
msgid ""
"The generic function :func:`copy.replace` also supports :class:`date` "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"A função genérica :func:`copy.replace` também suporta objetos :class:`date`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:747 ../../library/datetime.rst:1482
msgid ""
"Return a :class:`time.struct_time` such as returned by :func:`time."
"localtime`."
msgstr ""
"Devolve um :class:`time.struct_time` como o devolvido por :func:`time."
"localtime`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:749
msgid "The hours, minutes and seconds are 0, and the DST flag is -1."
msgstr "As horas, minutos e segundos são 0, e a flag DST é -1."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:751 ../../library/datetime.rst:1484
msgid "``d.timetuple()`` is equivalent to::"
msgstr "``d.timetuple()`` é equivalente a::"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:753
msgid ""
"time.struct_time((d.year, d.month, d.day, 0, 0, 0, d.weekday(), yday, -1))"
msgstr ""
"time.struct_time((d.ano, d.mês, d.dia, 0, 0, 0, d.weekday(), yday, -1))"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:755
msgid ""
"where ``yday = d.toordinal() - date(d.year, 1, 1).toordinal() + 1`` is the "
"day number within the current year starting with 1 for January 1st."
msgstr ""
"onde ``yday = d.toordinal() - date(d.year, 1, 1).toordinal() + 1`` é o "
"número do dia dentro do ano atual, começando em 1 para 1 de janeiro."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:761
msgid ""
"Return the proleptic Gregorian ordinal of the date, where January 1 of year "
"1 has ordinal 1. For any :class:`date` object ``d``, ``date.fromordinal(d."
"toordinal()) == d``."
msgstr ""
"Devolve o ordinal gregoriano proléptico da data, onde 1 de janeiro do ano 1 "
"tem o ordinal 1. Para qualquer objeto :class:`date` ``d``, ``date."
"fromordinal(d.toordinal()) == d``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:768
msgid ""
"Return the day of the week as an integer, where Monday is 0 and Sunday is 6. "
"For example, ``date(2002, 12, 4).weekday() == 2``, a Wednesday. See also :"
"meth:`isoweekday`."
msgstr ""
"Devolve o dia da semana como um inteiro, onde segunda-feira é 0 e domingo é "
"6. Por exemplo, ``date(2002, 12, 4).weekday() == 2``, uma quarta-feira. Veja "
"também :meth:`isoweekday`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:775
msgid ""
"Return the day of the week as an integer, where Monday is 1 and Sunday is 7. "
"For example, ``date(2002, 12, 4).isoweekday() == 3``, a Wednesday. See also :"
"meth:`weekday`, :meth:`isocalendar`."
msgstr ""
"Devolve o dia da semana como um inteiro, onde segunda-feira é 1 e domingo é "
"7. Por exemplo, ``date(2002, 12, 4).isoweekday() == 3``, uma quarta-feira. "
"Veja também :meth:`weekday`, :meth:`isocalendar`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:782
msgid ""
"Return a :term:`named tuple` object with three components: ``year``, "
"``week`` and ``weekday``."
msgstr ""
"Devolve um objeto :term:`named tuple` com três componentes: ``year``, "
"``week`` e ``weekday``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:785
msgid ""
"The ISO calendar is a widely used variant of the Gregorian calendar. [#]_"
msgstr ""
"O calendário ISO é uma variante amplamente utilizada do calendário "
"gregoriano. [#]_"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:787
msgid ""
"The ISO year consists of 52 or 53 full weeks, and where a week starts on a "
"Monday and ends on a Sunday. The first week of an ISO year is the first "
"(Gregorian) calendar week of a year containing a Thursday. This is called "
"week number 1, and the ISO year of that Thursday is the same as its "
"Gregorian year."
msgstr ""
"O ano ISO consiste em 52 ou 53 semanas completas, e onde uma semana começa "
"numa segunda-feira e termina num domingo. A primeira semana de um ano ISO é "
"a primeira semana do calendário (gregoriano) de um ano que contém uma quinta-"
"feira. Isto é chamado semana número 1, e o ano ISO dessa quinta-feira é o "
"mesmo que o seu ano gregoriano."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:792
msgid ""
"For example, 2004 begins on a Thursday, so the first week of ISO year 2004 "
"begins on Monday, 29 Dec 2003 and ends on Sunday, 4 Jan 2004::"
msgstr ""
"Por exemplo, 2004 começa numa quinta-feira, então a primeira semana do ano "
"ISO 2004 começa na segunda-feira, 29 de dezembro de 2003 e termina no "
"domingo, 4 de janeiro de 2004:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:795
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> dt.date(2003, 12, 29).isocalendar()\n"
"datetime.IsoCalendarDate(year=2004, week=1, weekday=1)\n"
">>> dt.date(2004, 1, 4).isocalendar()\n"
"datetime.IsoCalendarDate(year=2004, week=1, weekday=7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:801
msgid "Result changed from a tuple to a :term:`named tuple`."
msgstr "O resultado mudou de um tuplo para um :term:`named tuple`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:807
msgid ""
"Return a string representing the date in ISO 8601 format, ``YYYY-MM-DD``::"
msgstr ""
"Devolve uma string que representa a data no formato ISO 8601, ``YYYY-MM-DD``:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:809
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> dt.date(2002, 12, 4).isoformat()\n"
"'2002-12-04'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:816
msgid "For a date ``d``, ``str(d)`` is equivalent to ``d.isoformat()``."
msgstr "Para uma data ``d``, ``str(d)`` é equivalente a ``d.isoformat()``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:821
msgid "Return a string representing the date::"
msgstr "Devolve uma string que representa a data:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:823
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> dt.date(2002, 12, 4).ctime()\n"
"'Wed Dec  4 00:00:00 2002'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:827 ../../library/datetime.rst:1675
msgid "``d.ctime()`` is equivalent to::"
msgstr "``d.ctime()`` é equivalente a::"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:829 ../../library/datetime.rst:1677
msgid "time.ctime(time.mktime(d.timetuple()))"
msgstr "time.ctime(time.mktime(d.timetuple()))"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:831
msgid ""
"on platforms where the native C :c:func:`ctime` function (which :func:`time."
"ctime` invokes, but which :meth:`date.ctime` does not invoke) conforms to "
"the C standard."
msgstr ""
"em plataformas onde a função nativa C :c:func:`ctime` (que :func:`time."
"ctime` invoca, mas que :meth:`date.ctime` não invoca) está conforme o padrão "
"C."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:838
msgid ""
"Return a string representing the date, controlled by an explicit format "
"string. Format codes referring to hours, minutes or seconds will see 0 "
"values. See also :ref:`strftime-strptime-behavior` and :meth:`date."
"isoformat`."
msgstr ""
"Devolve uma string que representa a data, controlada por uma string de "
"formato explícita. Os códigos de formato que se referem a horas, minutos ou "
"segundos verão valores 0. Veja também :ref:`strftime-strptime-behavior` e :"
"meth:`date.isoformat`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:845
msgid ""
"Same as :meth:`.date.strftime`. This makes it possible to specify a format "
"string for a :class:`.date` object in :ref:`formatted string literals <f-"
"strings>` and when using :meth:`str.format`. See also :ref:`strftime-"
"strptime-behavior` and :meth:`date.isoformat`."
msgstr ""
"Igual a :meth:`.date.strftime`. Isto torna possível especificar uma string "
"de formato para um objeto :class:`.date` em :ref:`literais de string "
"formatadas <f-strings>` e ao usar :meth:`str.format`. Veja também :ref:"
"`strftime-strptime-behavior` e :meth:`date.isoformat`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:852
msgid "Examples of usage: :class:`!date`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:854
msgid "Example of counting days to an event::"
msgstr "Exemplo de contagem de dias até a um evento:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:856
msgid ""
">>> import time\n"
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> today = dt.date.today()\n"
">>> today\n"
"datetime.date(2007, 12, 5)\n"
">>> today == dt.date.fromtimestamp(time.time())\n"
"True\n"
">>> my_birthday = dt.date(today.year, 6, 24)\n"
">>> if my_birthday < today:\n"
"...     my_birthday = my_birthday.replace(year=today.year + 1)\n"
"...\n"
">>> my_birthday\n"
"datetime.date(2008, 6, 24)\n"
">>> time_to_birthday = abs(my_birthday - today)\n"
">>> time_to_birthday.days\n"
"202"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:873
msgid "More examples of working with :class:`date`:"
msgstr "Mais exemplos de trabalho com :class:`date`:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:875
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> d = dt.date.fromordinal(730920) # 730920th day after 1. 1. 0001\n"
">>> d\n"
"datetime.date(2002, 3, 11)\n"
"\n"
">>> # Methods related to formatting string output\n"
">>> d.isoformat()\n"
"'2002-03-11'\n"
">>> d.strftime(\"%d/%m/%y\")\n"
"'11/03/02'\n"
">>> d.strftime(\"%A %d. %B %Y\")\n"
"'Monday 11. March 2002'\n"
">>> d.ctime()\n"
"'Mon Mar 11 00:00:00 2002'\n"
">>> 'The {1} is {0:%d}, the {2} is {0:%B}.'.format(d, \"day\", \"month\")\n"
"'The day is 11, the month is March.'\n"
"\n"
">>> # Methods for extracting 'components' under different calendars\n"
">>> t = d.timetuple()\n"
">>> for i in t:\n"
"...     print(i)\n"
"2002                # year\n"
"3                   # month\n"
"11                  # day\n"
"0\n"
"0\n"
"0\n"
"0                   # weekday (0 = Monday)\n"
"70                  # 70th day in the year\n"
"-1\n"
">>> ic = d.isocalendar()\n"
">>> for i in ic:\n"
"...     print(i)\n"
"2002                # ISO year\n"
"11                  # ISO week number\n"
"1                   # ISO day number ( 1 = Monday )\n"
"\n"
">>> # A date object is immutable; all operations produce a new object\n"
">>> d.replace(year=2005)\n"
"datetime.date(2005, 3, 11)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:922
msgid ":class:`!datetime` objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:924
msgid ""
"A :class:`.datetime` object is a single object containing all the "
"information from a :class:`date` object and a :class:`.time` object."
msgstr ""
"Um objeto :class:`.datetime` é um único objeto que contém toda a informação "
"de um objeto :class:`date` e de um objeto :class:`.time`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:927
msgid ""
"Like a :class:`date` object, :class:`.datetime` assumes the current "
"Gregorian calendar extended in both directions; like a :class:`.time` "
"object, :class:`!datetime` assumes there are exactly 3600\\*24 seconds in "
"every day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:931
msgid "Constructor:"
msgstr "Construtor:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:935
msgid ""
"The *year*, *month* and *day* arguments are required. *tzinfo* may be "
"``None``, or an instance of a :class:`tzinfo` subclass. The remaining "
"arguments must be integers in the following ranges:"
msgstr ""
"Os argumentos *ano*, *mês* e *dia* são obrigatórios. *tzinfo* pode ser "
"``None``, ou uma instância de uma subclasse de :class:`tzinfo`. Os "
"argumentos restantes devem ser inteiros nos seguintes intervalos:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:939
msgid "``MINYEAR <= year <= MAXYEAR``,"
msgstr "``MINYEAR <= year <= MAXYEAR``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:940
msgid "``1 <= month <= 12``,"
msgstr "``1 <= month <= 12``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:941
msgid "``1 <= day <= number of days in the given month and year``,"
msgstr "``1 <= day <= number of days in the given month and year``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:942 ../../library/datetime.rst:1840
msgid "``0 <= hour < 24``,"
msgstr "``0 <= hour < 24``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:943 ../../library/datetime.rst:1841
msgid "``0 <= minute < 60``,"
msgstr "``0 <= minute < 60``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:944 ../../library/datetime.rst:1842
msgid "``0 <= second < 60``,"
msgstr "``0 <= second < 60``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:945 ../../library/datetime.rst:1843
msgid "``0 <= microsecond < 1000000``,"
msgstr "``0 <= microsecond < 1000000``,"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:946 ../../library/datetime.rst:1844
msgid "``fold in [0, 1]``."
msgstr "``fold in [0, 1]``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:950 ../../library/datetime.rst:1403
#: ../../library/datetime.rst:2008
msgid "Added the *fold* parameter."
msgstr "Adicionado o parâmetro *fold*."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:958
msgid "Return the current local date and time, with :attr:`.tzinfo` ``None``."
msgstr "Devolve a data e hora locais atuais, com :attr:`.tzinfo` ``None``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:960
msgid "Equivalent to::"
msgstr "Equivalente a::"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:962
msgid "datetime.fromtimestamp(time.time())"
msgstr "datetime.fromtimestamp(time.time())"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:964
msgid "See also :meth:`now`, :meth:`fromtimestamp`."
msgstr "Veja também :meth:`now`, :meth:`fromtimestamp`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:966
msgid ""
"This method is functionally equivalent to :meth:`now`, but without a ``tz`` "
"parameter."
msgstr ""
"Este método é funcionalmente equivalente a :meth:`now`, mas sem o parâmetro "
"``tz``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:972
msgid "Return the current local date and time."
msgstr "Devolve a data e hora locais atuais."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:974
msgid ""
"If optional argument *tz* is ``None`` or not specified, this is like :meth:"
"`today`, but, if possible, supplies more precision than can be gotten from "
"going through a :func:`time.time` timestamp (for example, this may be "
"possible on platforms supplying the C :c:func:`gettimeofday` function)."
msgstr ""
"Se o argumento opcional *tz* for ``None`` ou não for especificado, isto é "
"como :meth:`today`, mas, se possível, fornece mais precisão do que pode ser "
"obtido através de um timestamp :func:`time.time` (por exemplo, isto pode ser "
"possível em plataformas que fornecem a função C :c:func:`gettimeofday`)."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:980
msgid ""
"If *tz* is not ``None``, it must be an instance of a :class:`tzinfo` "
"subclass, and the current date and time are converted to *tz*’s time zone."
msgstr ""
"Se *tz* não for ``None``, deve ser uma instância de uma subclasse de :class:"
"`tzinfo`, e a data e hora atuais são convertidas para o fuso horário de *tz*."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:983
msgid "This function is preferred over :meth:`today` and :meth:`utcnow`."
msgstr "Esta função é preferível a :meth:`today` e :meth:`utcnow`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:987
msgid ""
"Subsequent calls to :meth:`!datetime.now` may return the same instant "
"depending on the precision of the underlying clock."
msgstr ""
"Chamadas subsequentes a :meth:`!datetime.now` podem devolver o mesmo "
"instante dependendo da precisão do relógio subjacente."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:993
msgid "Return the current UTC date and time, with :attr:`.tzinfo` ``None``."
msgstr "Devolve a data e hora UTC atuais, com :attr:`.tzinfo` ``None``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:995
msgid ""
"This is like :meth:`now`, but returns the current UTC date and time, as a "
"naive :class:`.datetime` object. An aware current UTC datetime can be "
"obtained by calling ``datetime.now(timezone.utc)``. See also :meth:`now`."
msgstr ""
"Isto é como :meth:`now`, mas devolve a data e hora UTC atuais, como um "
"objeto :class:`.datetime` ingénuo. Uma data e hora UTC atuais conscientes "
"podem ser obtidas chamando ``datetime.now(timezone.utc)``. Veja também :meth:"
"`now`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1001
msgid ""
"Because naive ``datetime`` objects are treated by many ``datetime`` methods "
"as local times, it is preferred to use aware datetimes to represent times in "
"UTC. As such, the recommended way to create an object representing the "
"current time in UTC is by calling ``datetime.now(timezone.utc)``."
msgstr ""
"Como os objetos ``datetime`` ingénuos são tratados por muitos métodos "
"``datetime`` como horas locais, é preferível usar datas/horas conscientes "
"para representar tempos em UTC. Assim, a forma recomendada de criar um "
"objeto que represente a hora atual em UTC é chamando ``datetime.now(timezone."
"utc)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1008
msgid "Use :meth:`datetime.now` with :const:`UTC` instead."
msgstr "Use :meth:`datetime.now` com :const:`UTC` em vez disso."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1013
msgid ""
"Return the local date and time corresponding to the POSIX timestamp, such as "
"is returned by :func:`time.time`. If optional argument *tz* is ``None`` or "
"not specified, the timestamp is converted to the platform's local date and "
"time, and the returned :class:`.datetime` object is naive."
msgstr ""
"Devolve a data e hora locais correspondentes ao timestamp POSIX, como o "
"devolvido por :func:`time.time`. Se o argumento opcional *tz* for ``None`` "
"ou não for especificado, o timestamp é convertido para a data e hora locais "
"da plataforma, e o objeto :class:`.datetime` devolvido é ingénuo."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1018
msgid ""
"If *tz* is not ``None``, it must be an instance of a :class:`tzinfo` "
"subclass, and the timestamp is converted to *tz*’s time zone."
msgstr ""
"Se *tz* não for ``None``, deve ser uma instância de uma subclasse de :class:"
"`tzinfo`, e o timestamp é convertido para o fuso horário de *tz*."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1021
msgid ""
":meth:`fromtimestamp` may raise :exc:`OverflowError`, if the timestamp is "
"out of the range of values supported by the platform C :c:func:`localtime` "
"or :c:func:`gmtime` functions, and :exc:`OSError` on :c:func:`localtime` or :"
"c:func:`gmtime` failure. It's common for this to be restricted to years in "
"1970 through 2038. Note that on non-POSIX systems that include leap seconds "
"in their notion of a timestamp, leap seconds are ignored by :meth:"
"`fromtimestamp`, and then it's possible to have two timestamps differing by "
"a second that yield identical :class:`.datetime` objects. This method is "
"preferred over :meth:`utcfromtimestamp`."
msgstr ""
":meth:`fromtimestamp` pode gerar um :exc:`OverflowError` se o timestamp "
"estiver fora do intervalo de valores suportados pelas funções C :c:func:"
"`localtime` ou :c:func:`gmtime` da plataforma, e um :exc:`OSError` em caso "
"de falha de :c:func:`localtime` ou :c:func:`gmtime`. É comum que isto esteja "
"restrito aos anos entre 1970 e 2038. Note que em sistemas não-POSIX que "
"incluem segundos bissextos na sua noção de timestamp, os segundos bissextos "
"são ignorados por :meth:`fromtimestamp`, e então é possível ter dois "
"timestamps que diferem por um segundo e que produzem objetos :class:`."
"datetime` idênticos. Este método é preferível a :meth:`utcfromtimestamp`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1032
msgid ""
"Raise :exc:`OverflowError` instead of :exc:`ValueError` if the timestamp is "
"out of the range of values supported by the platform C :c:func:`localtime` "
"or :c:func:`gmtime` functions. Raise :exc:`OSError` instead of :exc:"
"`ValueError` on :c:func:`localtime` or :c:func:`gmtime` failure."
msgstr ""
"Gera um :exc:`OverflowError` em vez de um :exc:`ValueError` se o timestamp "
"estiver fora do intervalo de valores suportados pelas funções C :c:func:"
"`localtime` ou :c:func:`gmtime` da plataforma. Gera um :exc:`OSError` em vez "
"de um :exc:`ValueError` em caso de falha de :c:func:`localtime` ou :c:func:"
"`gmtime`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1039
msgid ":meth:`fromtimestamp` may return instances with :attr:`.fold` set to 1."
msgstr ""
":meth:`fromtimestamp` pode devolver instâncias com :attr:`.fold` definido "
"como 1."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1048
msgid ""
"Return the UTC :class:`.datetime` corresponding to the POSIX timestamp, "
"with :attr:`.tzinfo` ``None``.  (The resulting object is naive.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1051
msgid ""
"This may raise :exc:`OverflowError`, if the timestamp is out of the range of "
"values supported by the platform C :c:func:`gmtime` function, and :exc:"
"`OSError` on :c:func:`gmtime` failure. It's common for this to be restricted "
"to years in 1970 through 2038."
msgstr ""
"Isto pode gerar um :exc:`OverflowError` se o timestamp estiver fora do "
"intervalo de valores suportados pela função C :c:func:`gmtime` da "
"plataforma, e um :exc:`OSError` em caso de falha de :c:func:`gmtime`. É "
"comum que isto esteja restrito aos anos entre 1970 e 2038."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1056
msgid "To get an aware :class:`.datetime` object, call :meth:`fromtimestamp`::"
msgstr ""
"Para obter um objeto :class:`.datetime` consciente, chame :meth:"
"`fromtimestamp`::"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1058
msgid "datetime.fromtimestamp(timestamp, timezone.utc)"
msgstr "datetime.fromtimestamp(timestamp, timezone.utc)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1060
msgid ""
"On the POSIX compliant platforms, it is equivalent to the following "
"expression::"
msgstr ""
"Em plataformas compatíveis com POSIX, é equivalente à seguinte expressão:"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1063
msgid ""
"datetime(1970, 1, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc) + timedelta(seconds=timestamp)"
msgstr ""
"datetime(1970, 1, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc) + timedelta(seconds=timestamp)"

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1065
msgid ""
"except the latter formula always supports the full years range: between :"
"const:`MINYEAR` and :const:`MAXYEAR` inclusive."
msgstr ""
"exceto que a última fórmula suporta sempre o intervalo completo de anos: "
"entre :const:`MINYEAR` e :const:`MAXYEAR`, inclusive."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1070
msgid ""
"Because naive ``datetime`` objects are treated by many ``datetime`` methods "
"as local times, it is preferred to use aware datetimes to represent times in "
"UTC. As such, the recommended way to create an object representing a "
"specific timestamp in UTC is by calling ``datetime.fromtimestamp(timestamp, "
"tz=timezone.utc)``."
msgstr ""
"Como os objetos ``datetime`` ingénuos são tratados por muitos métodos "
"``datetime`` como horas locais, é preferível usar datas/horas conscientes "
"para representar tempos em UTC. Assim, a forma recomendada de criar um "
"objeto que represente um timestamp específico em UTC é chamando ``datetime."
"fromtimestamp(timestamp, tz=timezone.utc)``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1076
msgid ""
"Raise :exc:`OverflowError` instead of :exc:`ValueError` if the timestamp is "
"out of the range of values supported by the platform C :c:func:`gmtime` "
"function. Raise :exc:`OSError` instead of :exc:`ValueError` on :c:func:"
"`gmtime` failure."
msgstr ""
"Gera um :exc:`OverflowError` em vez de um :exc:`ValueError` se o timestamp "
"estiver fora do intervalo de valores suportados pela função C :c:func:"
"`gmtime` da plataforma. Gera um :exc:`OSError` em vez de um :exc:"
"`ValueError` em caso de falha de :c:func:`gmtime`."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1087
msgid "Use :meth:`datetime.fromtimestamp` with :const:`UTC` instead."
msgstr "Use :meth:`datetime.fromtimestamp` com :const:`UTC` em vez disso."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1092
msgid ""
"Return the :class:`.datetime` corresponding to the proleptic Gregorian "
"ordinal, where January 1 of year 1 has ordinal 1. :exc:`ValueError` is "
"raised unless ``1 <= ordinal <= datetime.max.toordinal()``. The hour, "
"minute, second and microsecond of the result are all 0, and :attr:`.tzinfo` "
"is ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Devolve o :class:`.datetime` correspondente ao ordinal gregoriano "
"proléptico, onde 1 de janeiro do ano 1 tem o ordinal 1. :exc:`ValueError` é "
"gerado a menos que ``1 <= ordinal <= datetime.max.toordinal()``. A hora, "
"minuto, segundo e microsegundo do resultado são todos 0, e :attr:`.tzinfo` é "
"``None``."

#: ../../library/datetime.rst:1100
msgid ""
"Return a new :class:`.datetime` object whose date components are equal to "
"the given :class:`date` object's, and whose time components are equal to the "
"given :class:`.time` object's. If the *tzinfo* argument is provided, its "
"value is used to set the :attr:`.tzinfo` attribute of the result, otherwise "
